<title>FINLAND: UPM-Kymmene says profits decline from record level.</title>
<headline>UPM-Kymmene says profits decline from record level.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI, Finland</dateline>
<text>
<p>UPM-Kymmene Oy, Europe's largest forestry group, said Tuesday that its 1996 profits fell by 43 percent from the previous year's record level.</p>
<p>The company said profits before extraordinary items fell to 3.56 billion markka ($698 million) from a record 6.28 billion ($1.23 billion) in 1995.</p>
<p>It added that net sales fell to 51.75 billion markka ($10.2 billion) from 54.74 billion ($10.7 billion).</p>
